    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d663">

                <pb facs="0844" n="732" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg732"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.512/1993</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Fletcher</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-06-13T10:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 13, 1918, 10 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1170. The Mexican Government has ordered publication full text of note of April
                    2, protesting against petroleum decree and all papers carry it to-day with
                    display headlines. <hi rendition="#italic">Pueblo</hi>, official mouthpiece,
                    heads it “President Wilson threatens Mexico”; <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Democrata’s</hi> head in red letters is “The Government of the United
                    States threatens to intervene in Mexico if its pretensions are not
                    satisfied.”</p>
                <p>The publication of our protest at this time by the Government looks like an
                    attempt to offset and destroy effect of the President’s recent speech,<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d663-f1"/> and an endeavor to tie our hands in regard to
                    petroleum decree.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Fletcher</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
